{
  "id": "global-health",
  "title": "Global health charities, by GiveWell funding gap",
  "summary": "Top-charity funding gaps — bednets, malaria chemoprevention, vitamin A, vaccine incentives, deworming and cash — sized and valued with GiveWell's 2021 cost-effectiveness estimates (1× = a dollar of cash to GiveDirectly). Lens adjustments and funders are illustrative, not GiveWell's.",
  "valueUnit": "value per $ in multiples of cash (GiveDirectly = 1×)",
  "sources": [
    {
      "name": "GiveWell — 2021 top-charity cost-effectiveness analysis (funding gaps 2021-2023)",
      "url": "https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1g_dfZa6xciKkMiiUPVAF02CQLSVHULFpjP5wN7FrpSI/edit"
    },
    {
      "name": "GiveWell — Cost-effectiveness models (current and past versions)",
      "url": "https://www.givewell.org/how-we-work/our-criteria/cost-effectiveness/cost-effectiveness-models"
    }
  ],
  "assumptions": {
    "under_review_weight": 0.5,
    "non_mortality_value_weight": 0.25,
    "within_gap_slope": 0.25,
    "note": "All cost-effectiveness numbers, funding-gap sizes, shares of value from averted deaths and costs per life saved are GiveWell's, from its 2021 cost-effectiveness workbook (funding gaps for 2021-2023); they are dated and not current GiveWell recommendations. Choices made here: (1) one application per funding gap, except Helen Keller's four Nigerian state gaps and SCI Foundation's four yearly tranches, which share one GiveWell estimate and are each combined into one application; (2) GiveWell gives one estimate per gap, so it is used as the average over the gap, with value falling linearly from 1.25x to 0.75x of it across the gap (best-targeted areas first) — the shape is illustrative, the average is GiveWell's; (3) GiveDirectly appears only with its $23.5M 'maintain rolling programs' gap, as the cash benchmark — its scale-up gaps ($432M) and a Sightsavers survey gap GiveWell only assesses qualitatively are left out; (4) the Evidence strength lens counts gaps GiveWell marks as still under investigation at 0.5x — an illustrative discount, not GiveWell's; (5) the Lives saved first lens keeps the share of value GiveWell attributes to averted deaths and counts the rest (income and development gains) at 0.25x, also illustrative; (6) the funders and their budgets are fictional."
  },
